# Every text file is LF on every OS. Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true system-wide, so a plain
# clone there checked out every .sh/.py as CRLF (2026-10-13); this wins over that setting, and a CRLF
# save from a Windows editor is normalized at commit. Binaries (media, fonts, models) are detected and
# left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
